<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Sept numbers in work fall yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Sept numbers in work fall yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics</p>
<p>Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN</p>
<p>NUMBERS IN WORK		Sept 96   Aug 96  Sept 95</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(unadj, million)    34.770   34.450   35.146</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(seas adj, million) 34.409   34.448   34.780</p>
<p> Number in work (2)(seas adj, million) 34.463   34.497   34.821</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj,million)	  28.430   28.168   28.731</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)    28.148   28.179   28.444</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj, million)	  6.409    6.343    6.470</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)     6.315    6.318    6.377</p>
<p>NOTE - Pan-German figure marked (1) refer to people living</p>
<p>in Germany. Those marked (2), as well as all the west and east</p>
<p>German figures, refer to people working in the respective</p>
<p>regions but not necessarily living in Germany.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
